.TH GPE 1 "1970-1-1" "v1.0" "Custom Scripts Manual"
.SH NAME
gpe \- update all git repositories in the current directory in parallel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gpe
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gpe
is a batch update utility that scans the immediate subdirectories of the current 
working directory for Git repositories and executes
.MR git-pull 1
on each.
.PP
To optimize performance, the script processes up to 8 repositories 
simultaneously. It provides a colorized, synchronized output to ensure that 
the status of each repository remains readable despite the parallel execution.
.SH FEATURES
.TP
.B Parallel Execution
Uses job control to manage a maximum of 8 concurrent background processes.
.TP
.B Output Synchronization
Uses
.MR flock 1
to ensure that the multi-line output from different repositories does not 
interleave in the terminal.
.TP
.B Error Reporting
Maintains a temporary log of failed updates and presents a detailed summary 
upon completion, listing exactly which repositories encountered errors.
.SH OUTPUT
The script provides a visual status for each directory:
.TP
.B \[u2713] (Green Check)
Indicates the repository was updated successfully.
.TP
.B \[u2717] (Red X)
Indicates that the
.B git pull
command failed (e.g., due to merge conflicts, network issues, or local changes).
.SH NOTES
The script ignores any directory that does not contain a 
.I .git 
subfolder. It uses
.MR mktemp 1
to create lock files and failure logs, which are automatically cleaned up 
on exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.MR git 1 ,
.MR git-pull 1 ,
.MR flock 1 ,
.MR wait 1
